    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d617">

                <pb facs="0726" n="654" xml:id="pg654"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 66/40.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Belgian
                    Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-06-02"><hi rendition="#italic">June 2,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 514.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 25th ultimo, by which you inform me, under instructions from
                    your Government, that September 28 next has been finally fixed as the date for
                    the opening of the International Conference on Maritime Law at Brussels.</p>
                <p>Thanking you for this information, I beg to assure you, in reply to the inquiry
                    contained in your note, that the Government of the United States will be pleased
                    to take part in this conference, the Congress of the United States having at its
                    last session made provision for such representation.</p>
                <p>I shall, in due season, be pleased to communicate to you the names of the
                    delegate or delegates who may be selected to represent the Government of the
                    United States in the conference.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
